randomCanonicalCurveGenus8with8Points -- Compute a random canonical curve of genus 8 with 8 marked point
********************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (I,idealsOfPts)=randomCanonicalCurveGenus8with8Points S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, homogeneous
        coordinate ring of $\PP^7$
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a canonical curve C of genus 8
      * idealsOfPts, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 8 ideals of K-rational
        points on C

Description
===========

According to Mukai [Mu] any smooth curve of genus 8 and Clifford index 3 is the
transversal intersection $C=\PP^7 \cap\ G(2,6) \subset \ \PP^{15}$. In
particular this is true for the general curve of genus 8. Picking 8 points in
the Grassmannian $G(2,6)$ at random and \PP^7 as their span gives the result.



